From 70153f5176c788fd96cde5caeeee9d21390fe674 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@nggconsult.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:33:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Draw the frame at device resolution

The canvas rendered at the 720-wide design box and the browser stretched it to the
screen: a 1.5x upscale of every outline and letter on a 2.75x phone, the softness
docs/VISUAL_AUDIT.md recorded as a deliberate, unmeasured decision.

renderScale (config/design.ts) now works out that upscale from the device pixel ratio
and the parent's size, clamped to [1, RENDER_SCALE_MAX], and createGameConfig hands the
Scale Manager the design box multiplied by it, so one logical pixel lands on one device
pixel. Every scene lays out from s and the Viewport and follows on its own; the particle
presets in ui/feedback.ts were the one thing sized outside s and are scaled as each
emitter is made.

RENDER_SCALE_MAX is the single constant to tune from a handset. 1 restores the previous
behaviour exactly. Fill cost is not yet measured on a mid-range Android.
